{% endif %}
| coinbase data | {{ crosslink_miner_extra_coinbase_data | default('(default)', true) }} |

- {{ crosslink_miner_threads }} solver thread{{ '' if crosslink_miner_threads | int == 1 else 's' }} (`crosslink_miner_threads`), {{ 'low' if crosslink_miner_low_priority | bool else 'normal' }} priority, about 144 MB each.
- Mining starts only after the node is synced. A syncing node is not broken.
{% if node_miner_shielded | default(false) | bool %}
- Rewards are shielded: every block pays one Ironwood note to this wallet's own unified address (the payout address above). The chain shows no address they went to, and a stake from this wallet spends those notes, so it shows none either.
- Rewards go to this node's own wallet: the seed above. Its 24-word phrase is in the key bundle, not on this host. Losing the seed loses the rewards.
- A note is spendable 3 blocks after the block that pays it (the wallet's own rule, `wallet_spendable_funds`).
{% else %}
- Rewards are spendable {{ crosslink_coinbase_maturity }} blocks after the block that pays them on this feature-net (Zcash: 100).
{% if not crosslink_miner_address %}
- Rewards go to this node's own wallet: the seed above. Its 24-word phrase is in the key bundle, not on this host. Losing the seed loses the rewards.
{% else %}
- Rewards go to the address in the inventory. This host holds no money.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if node_rewards is defined and not (node_miner_shielded | default(false) | bool) %}
- At {{ node_rewards.read_at }} the payout address had received {{ node_rewards.text.received }} cTAZ in {{ node_rewards.text.transactions }} transactions; balance {{ node_rewards.text.balance }} cTAZ. The full figures are in the key bundle's `rewards.json`.
{% endif %}

To read the rewards now, on this host:

{% if node_miner_shielded | default(false) | bool %}
```bash
curl -s -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"wallet_spendable_funds","params":[]}' \
  http://{{ crosslink_rpc_listen }}/            # spendable, pending and committed notes, in zatoshis (1 cTAZ = 100000000)
```

What the wallet received in total is not on the chain to read; `sudo crosslink-check` shows what it holds now.
{% else %}
```bash
curl -s -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"getaddressbalance","params":[{"addresses":["{{ node_miner_address | default('<payout address>', true) }}"]}]}' \
  http://{{ crosslink_rpc_listen }}/            # balance and received, in zatoshis (1 cTAZ = 100000000)
```
{% endif %}

From the control machine: `ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml rewards.yml -l {{ inventory_hostname }}`.
{% endif %}

