## Check

```bash
sudo crosslink-check                    # one screen: services, sync, peers, finality, seat, mining, wallet, stakes
sudo crosslink-check --json             # the same for a script
{% if not crosslink_disable_wallet | bool %}
sudo crosslink-stake --to <zfinv1…> --all --dry-run   # would a stake of the rewards go ahead?
{% endif %}
systemctl status {{ crosslink_service_name }}
journalctl -u {{ crosslink_service_name }} -f                                  # sync
{% if crosslink_mining_enabled | bool %}
journalctl -u {{ crosslink_service_name }} -f | grep -E 'mining|template'      # mining
{% endif %}
curl -s -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"getblockcount","params":[]}' \
  http://{{ crosslink_rpc_listen }}/            # RPC
```

## Rebuild

{% if crosslink_mining_enabled | bool %}
Provision a host and put it in the same groups. Create `{{ node_seed_path | dirname }}` owned by `{{ crosslink_user }}` and copy `secret.seed` from the key bundle into it **before the first start**, then run the playbook. Without the seed the node mines to a new address and the old rewards are stranded.
{% else %}
Provision a host, put it in the same groups, run the playbook. Nothing to restore: the chain state resyncs and the seed is regenerated.
{% endif %}
